{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/449626-a-game-in-istanbul-looking-for-material","id":449626,"title":"A game in Istanbul : looking for material","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-19T13:00:09-07:00","id":449626,"title":"A game in Istanbul : looking for material","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I'm starting a Demon game for the first time. I'm bored of the traditionnal occidental cities - special american ones - and I'm very excited that Demon Seed takes a side on east europe and Istanbul.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna set the game in Istanbul and follow the seed proposed in the pdf, but I have trouble to find some details about the city itself : I don't want to do a big sandoxing, just looking to some key locations or places and NPC that just can give the flavor of the city. Not looking to be simulationnating, just want to give an evocative feeling of Istanbul to the players.<br /> <br /> Any ideas ? Movies ? Books ? Websites","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/824-araknee","name":"Araknee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T18:12:58-07:00","id":452195,"title":"","content":"Books --<br /> <br /> Istanbul Intrigues by Barry Rubin -- nonfiction account of spying in the city during the second World War, read this if you read nothing else.<br /> The Black Book and Instanbul: Memories of the city -- by Orhan Pahuk<br /> <br /> <br /> TV --<br /> the discovery channel did a special on the city <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n_tyich_dxY\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n_tyich_dxY</a> --- Not thrilling scholarship but it give you some good visuals that will hep you describe scenes for your players<br /> <br /> <br /> Film -- Distant (Uzek) by Nuri Bilge Ceylan (director) Warning. This one is <i>slow</i>. Watch if you enjoy art house films.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T14:30:31-07:00","id":453163,"title":"","content":"Very nice, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/824-araknee","name":"Araknee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}